.TH EVENT_LOOP_REG_COUNT 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
event_loop_reg_count \- number of currently-registered event_reg handles
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

size_t event_loop_reg_count(event_loop loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the number of live registrations (event_loop_add() calls not yet
removed), not the number of epoll interest-list entries: one fd with
both directions registered counts as 2, since it is backed by two
independent event_reg handles sharing one entry.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  event_loop to query.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns the registration count on success.
Returns (size_t)-1 if loop is NULL.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call concurrently with event_loop_add(), event_loop_remove(),
and dispatch on the reactor thread; returns a consistent snapshot taken
under the loop's internal lock.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR event_loop_add (3),
.BR event_loop_remove (3)
